{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/15516-table-cannon","id":15516,"title":"Table Cannon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T12:13:21-08:00","id":15516,"title":"Table Cannon","content":"I don't know about you guys, but I have developed a fairly extensive table cannon over the years that ties together every game I have ever run or played in across all three settings. Looking back some of my favorite parts of the world my players and I have built were only inspired by the setting, and are nowhere to be found in any of the books. However, now that this new edition is pending, and tweaks are being made to the world and the setting I've started wondering &quot;should I take this opportunity to 'reboot' my table?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm sure you all have table cannon of your own, are any of you thinking of rebooting, or do you tend to keep your Continuum stories more independent of one another?<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:36:11-08:00","id":15630,"title":"","content":"Usually, I would do a reboot. I will be doing that for the Scion game when 2nd Edition comes out and I will also do it for Exalted 3rd edition when it comes out. Since my group has never done a full on sweeping campaign of all three games, then I do not have to worry about it when it comes to TC. My overall suggestion is to wipe clean and do it all over from the beginning.<br /> <br /> I have a few problem players. One is a rules lawyer who likes to stay ahead of the game and reads every single supplement so that he can know all the rules. This tends to make him come up with instances where he subconsciously does things that will help him win (and yes, he believes he can win in an RPG). Another one does his level best to not use out of character knowledge while he is in character but he fails.<br /> <br /> The best way to combat this is to come up with new things such as new powers and new things in the setting. So, I will go ahead and do my own reboots and do some alterations of the setting to throw them off the beaten path. The first one can be brought back down with the inclusion of new things and the second when he is not as familiar with the setting.<br /> <br /> Also, I have less selfish reasons to do a reboot. The main one is the fact that it gives me a tabula rasa. If there is something that I did not like from the previous settings, I can just go &quot;Well, to hell with that&quot; and likewise, if I loved something? &quot;Dude, I can do even better this time&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T14:37:59-08:00","id":16289,"title":"","content":"Table Cannon.<br /> <br /> Extensive Table Cannon?<br /> <br /> Mwahahah. I swear you're doing that on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 11-22-2013, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T16:49:26-08:00","id":17382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/15516-table-cannon?p=15630#post15630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually, I would do a reboot. I will be doing that for the Scion game when 2nd Edition comes out and I will also do it for Exalted 3rd edition when it comes out. Since my group has never done a full on sweeping campaign of all three games, then I do not have to worry about it when it comes to TC. My overall suggestion is to wipe clean and do it all over from the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Exalted 3e</b> has some rather significant cosmological changes, or so I hear (new Exalts and the like).<br /> <br /> <b>Scion</b> will be receiving a fairly substantial setting reboot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:20:24-08:00","id":18615,"title":"","content":"Most of the games I run tend to drift out into the fringes fairly quickly so my group used quite a bit of table canon though it was mostly little pieces here and there as gap fillers and not some kind of major rewrite (though over time it could seem like it was, especially where a supplement turns out to have gone a different route than we did).<br /> <br /> I only had Aberrant and Aeon Trinity and it was some time before I ran across information on the Hammersmith incident and the other Adventure! plot elements; the unique (and intriguing) double-blind way the core books (especially Aberrant) were written meant that a lot of the assumptions my initial campaign set was based on were somewhat different from the ones the game designers intended.<br /> <br /> The fact that the (Aberrant) team teleporter, Vortex, had those Dr. Who navigation moments fairly frequently so they ended up in some really strange places contributed to the drift quite a bit, especially when one of those errant wormholes landed them in the Aeon Trinity era for a short time (briefly meeting the PCs from that part of the campaign timeline though they never had the time to actually stop and talk with each other). When they got back they started trying to derail what they saw as a civilization crash and keep the world on the path to a brighter future which of course meant they were inadvertently working against Mercer\u2019s plan often as not, even though both sides were nominally the \u201cgood guys\u201d.<br /> <br /> Misunderstandings about their clashes with Proteus also got them in a lot of trouble and classified as part of the Aberrant faction even though they had little to do with them. Probably the biggest departure from canon was that the groups nemesis was a mysterious Nova-drug lord who would eventually go on to be The Colony as his taint built up to a critical threshold (I still do not know the canon origin story of him/it).<br /> <br /> I usually did not \u201creboot\u201d campaigns once they get going when new rules come out though I usually do try to translate them to the new system if it looks like it might be better and often end up with something in between if it seems that it will fit the established campaign continuity. Other times I pick a few threads and systems from the new to incorporate into the older one. Rarely would I jump to the new one and cut the continuity threads that do not fit with the new version (the longest running campaign I have had in any system was done in one of the very early superhero RPGs that went through some major changes over the years and I translated everything over numerous times rather than the easier route of scrapping and starting over for example). This has caused some odd situations in cases where the official systems and metaplot change radically from edition to edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","user":"BC001","date":". 11-27-2013, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:39:17-08:00","id":18628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/15516-table-cannon?p=18615#post18615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably the biggest departure from canon was that the groups nemesis was a mysterious Nova-drug lord who would eventually go on to be The Colony as his taint built up to a critical threshold (I still do not know the canon origin story of him/it).</div> </div> </div> </div>There is none. That was an intentional choice, so individual groups could do exactly what yours did: make the Colony whoever would best suit their purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T15:23:21-08:00","id":20820,"title":"","content":"I play a post-Speech Divis Mal and a post-death Slider at the journal-based Milliways Bar RP over on Dreamwidth, and I'm holding off on plans to reboot either one until I find out whether they even <i>have</i> counterparts in the TC. That's all I know at this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}